{"at": "2026-07-10T19:35:41Z", "commit_ref": "3733a1a", "decision": "include", "gate": "build", "rationale": "Every part (A-N) edits F# sources and project files under Berreman/: Part B relocates the workbench into OpticalConstructor.Ui and adds OpticalConstructor.TestWindows.App to Berreman.slnx, Part M adds OpticalConstructor.Database (C#) and OpticalConstructor.Seeding, and section 0.6 mandates a zero-warning Release build with no MSB3277 regression."}
{"at": "2026-07-10T19:35:41Z", "commit_ref": "3733a1a", "decision": "include", "gate": "unit-tests", "rationale": "The spec plans no solver code change, but Part K consumes solver surfaces (Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs:671 Polder mu, OpticalProperties/Active.fs:152 gyration) and Parts B/N reshape the solution graph and run a solution-wide warning sweep; the BerremanTests suite guards the solver against accidental regression (inclusion bias applies)."}
{"at": "2026-07-10T19:35:41Z", "commit_ref": "3733a1a", "decision": "include", "gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "rationale": "Sections 0.3/0.4 mandate pure Domain/Storage behaviour tests in OpticalConstructor.Tests: the faceted engine + 1-2-5 bucketing (Part D), settings record (C), protected entries + PolarizerBehavior (F), Select-mode context (G), lifecycle versioning rule (H), experiment setup + scene/experiment proxy round-trips (I), out-of-band computation (J), strict v1 CSV parsers behind ExperimentDataProxy (L), and the EFC SQLite proof + seeding push (M). No new test project is introduced, so this gate covers all of it."}
{"at": "2026-07-10T19:35:41Z", "commit_ref": "3733a1a", "decision": "include", "gate": "ui-smoke", "rationale": "Section 0.4 requires every new surface to render headless; Part B relocates the live workbench into OpticalConstructor.Ui (the gate's applies_to paths), Parts E/F/G/K/L add the Materials, Library, and SolverHandoff windows plus reworked editors, and Part N's closing WIRE_UI step drives the whole surface headless."}
{"at": "2026-07-10T19:35:41Z", "commit_ref": "3733a1a", "decision": "include", "gate": "ui-tests", "rationale": "Per-panel Avalonia.Headless view tests in OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests cover the FacetedTree control and Materials window (E), Library window + Select mode buttons (F/G), table binding visuals and out-of-band badge (J), tabbed editor charts + unsaved-edit confirmation (K), inverse flow + handoff window (L), and the four-button launcher row with consolidated automation ids (N). Part A's keyed-row/AutomationId sweep is exactly the hygiene these tests exercise."}
